    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on a pod in our GKE cluster. it's a microservice running on a standard node pool. here are the logs from the last few restarts:\n\n`Error: failed to bind to port 8080: address already in use`\n`liveness probe failed: HTTP probe failed with statuscode: 500`\n\ncan you give me a diagnostic checklist to figure out if this is a resource issue, a probe misconfig, or something else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This error strongly suggests a conflict within the container itself rather than a general cluster issue. First, check the application logs *before* the crash to see if a prior instance is still running or failing to stop cleanly. Verify that your container is configured to gracefully shut down when stopped, preventing port conflicts on restart. Finally, confirm the liveness probe path and expected response code match what your service is actually serving on port 8080.",
      "source": "target",
