    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the metrics look okay for now, memory hasn't peaked. \n\nso if it's not resources, i'm thinking it's either a bad liveness probe or some weird networking thing where the port isn't being released properly. can you help me write a quick debug script or a temporary manifest change to test if changing the probe interval or the port helps isolate the issue?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To test the probe, temporarily increase the `initialDelaySeconds` significantly in your Pod spec, giving the application ample time to bind before the liveness check begins. If that resolves the immediate crash, the application needs longer to boot. Alternatively, briefly change the probe port to something non-standard (e.g., 8081) to fully isolate if the issue is strictly related to port 8080 binding.",
      "source": "target",
